read_csv() is an R/qtl2 function that is intended for its specific format of files, with an initial column of individual identifiers that will become the row names. Best to use the built-in function read.csv, or to use data.table::fread(), as you did for the vcf file.

If you're just trying to measure distances among the RIL, I would skip trying to use R/qtl2 and just calculate the proportion of genotype mismatches between lines.

karl

