The re-encoding of the genotypes would be used to get the files into the format needed for R/qtl2, to be read with read_cross2().

The compare_geno() function takes as input a "cross2" object, which is the output of read_cross2().
The error "unused argument (cross2="riself")" is because compare_geno() doesn't have an argument named cross2; it's not at all clear what you're trying to do with cross2="riself".

calc_kinship() isn't the next step in this. calc_kinship() takes genotype probabilities as input, which would be produced with the calc_genoprob() function.

karl

